# Least-used requirements-documentation formats in ML-enabled system projects

## Hypothesis (answer)
**ML Canvas and BDD scenarios are the two least-used documentation formats for requirements of
ML-enabled system projects.** In this survey file, ML Canvas was reported as used by 15/194 = 7.73%
of respondents (95% bootstrap percentile CI 4.12-11.86; Wilson 4.74-12.36) and BDD scenarios by
4/194 = 2.06% (percentile CI 0.52-4.12; Wilson 0.81-5.18) - the two lowest of the ten named
formats, against 34.02% for notebooks, 32.47% user stories and 26.29% requirements lists. The
ordering is robust: over 20,000 respondent-level bootstrap replicates BDD scenarios is the least-used
format in 99.9% of replicates and ML Canvas the second least-used in 97.5% of replicates (candidate
pool = 10 named formats). If the unspecified "Others" free-text residual is left in the pool it ties
ML Canvas at 15/194 and the second-least probability splits 53.6% (ML Canvas) / 45.6% (Others), which
is why the residual - and the "Not Documented" response option (30/194 = 15.46%), a statement of
non-documentation rather than a format - are excluded from the format ranking. A keyword audit of all
14 "Others" free texts found 0 aliases for any named format (Confluence/Jira/Notion/wiki/GitHub,
design docs, meeting notes, "mathematical models"), so nothing was folded out of the ranking.
The ranking is unchanged on every sensitivity base: all 276 stored rows (ML Canvas 5.43%, BDD 1.45%),
Completed-family only (8.0% / 2.13%), answered-and-named-at-least-one-format (10.27% / 2.74%),
answered with Duration>0 (8.33% / 2.38%) and project-weighted by D7_Total_ML_Projects.

**Provenance caveat.** The magnitudes quoted in the question (10.13%, 95% CI [9.926, 10.333];
4.366%, 95% CI [4.231, 4.501]) are NOT reproducible from this file and are not claimed here: no
denominator in the file yields both values (the ratio 10.13/4.366 = 2.32 is unreachable from the
observed 15:4 = 3.75), and the CI half-widths imply an effective sample size of ~84,000-88,000,
which exceeds the 55,752 cells the file contains. This is consistent with a different data version or
a project-level expansion in the source. Our results are consistent with the quoted claim in
*identity and ordering* - ML Canvas first (higher share), BDD scenarios second (absolute minimum) -
while our respondent-level percentages are lower.

## Reproduction
`python3 analysis/q10_bootstrap.py` (python 3.12.14, pandas 3.0.2, numpy 2.4.4, scipy 1.16.0,
seed 20261025, B = 10,000 CIs / 20,000 rank probabilities; byte-identical output on rerun).
Definitions: "used" == item value `quoted`; `-77` == item non-response -> respondent excluded
(negative sentinel codes -66/-77/-99 are NA and are never counted as responses); unit of resampling =
respondent row (full Q10 response vector); headline CI = percentile, with Wilson and basic reported.
